For ChangedUrl to Studio with tab: set studio state. If tab is undefined, should we reset to chat? If navigating to bare `/studio`, canonical semantics: default tab chat. But user tab selection via clicks doesn't change URL; if they navigate away and back to /studio, current code preserves selected tab. Is that "stale"? Probably okay. For determinism, I'd set tab from URL only when explicitly provided (`tab !== undefined`), leaving state otherwise. So `/studio` → preserves/default chat; `/studio?tab=audio` → forced audio. Legacy `/app/studio/audio` redirects to `/studio?tab=audio` → init sets audio. Good.

